      "markdown": "thus Eq. (S16) holds and _B_ ( _x, rx_ )<sup>_S_</sup> is a Lipschitz cap. **Theorem 2 (Convergence via Lipschitz Caps)** _Given the tightness factor µ >_ 1 _, the set of all sampled points V and the sample maximum m_ ¯ _j,V_ = max _x∈V dj_ ( _x_ ) _. Let the initial ball maximum be defined by m_<sup>_⋆_</sup> _j_<sup>= max</sup><sup>_x∈B_</sup> 0<sup>_dj_(</sup><sup>_x_)</sup><sup>_. Then:_</sup> _∀γ ∈_ (0 _,_ 1) _, ∃N ∈_ N _s.t._ Pr( _µ · m_ ¯ _j,V ≥ m_<sup>_⋆_</sup> _j_<sup>)</sup><sup>_≥_1</sup><sup>_−γ_</sup> (S31)",
